From 09d62622091b59532b5a277adfab26a598f78ddf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 15:43:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 022/638] gl: select EGL for the native AROS backend [chromium]
 [aros]

AI_PHASE: chromium-headless-bringup

AI_STATUS: done

ROOT_CAUSE: Chromium's ui/gl component assumes EGL supplies its display types, binding declarations, and DisplayKey integration on supported platforms. AROS was omitted from use_egl, so the component compiled its EGL implementation sources without USE_EGL and produced a cascade of missing types and symbols.

FIX_REASON: Enable the existing EGL backend for AROS rather than adding header guards around an internally EGL-based component. This aligns the browser graph with the Mesa/VirGL/RadeonSI stack while retaining runtime software or disabled-GPU operation for initial headless tests.

SCOPE: ui/gl GN feature selection.

VALIDATION: filtered GN regeneration succeeded; ninja -C out/aros-headless -j4 obj/ui/gl/gl/gl_display.o obj/ui/gl/gl/gl_display_manager.o

RISK: medium; the graph now compiles additional EGL code whose final AROS loader and runtime integration still require link and boot validation.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
---
 ui/gl/features.gni | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ui/gl/features.gni b/ui/gl/features.gni
index cd5c6d2de1..f81a3e5826 100644
--- a/ui/gl/features.gni
+++ b/ui/gl/features.gni
@@ -14,7 +14,8 @@ declare_args() {
   # Should EGL support be compiled?
   # Can be overriden to test during bring up of EGL support on other platforms.
   use_egl =
-      is_win || is_android || is_linux || is_chromeos || is_fuchsia || is_apple
+      is_win || is_android || is_aros || is_linux || is_chromeos ||
+      is_fuchsia || is_apple
 
   # Should Dawn support be compiled to back the WebGPU implementation?
   # Also controls linking Dawn dependencies in such as SPIRV-Tools/SPIRV-Cross.
